topics.detail:
Starlink Restriction argues that Musk suggested slowing down Ukraine's Starlink service. Musk and Trump conspired to throttle back Starlink speeds to Ukraine. Drone Attacks argues that Ukrainian drones attacked Russia. Russian drones attacked Ukraine. Drones disrupted air traffic in Russia.

@kyivindependent.com: “⚡️️️️️️️Musk suggested Trump restrict Ukraine's Starlink service, Telegraph reports. Four sources familiar with the discussion said that Elon Musk approached U.S. President Donald Trump with the idea of slowing down Ukraine's Starlink service on the battlefield.”

Starlink Restriction (82.3%) says Musk and Trump restricted Ukraine's Starlink service. Drone Attacks (17.7%) says Drones are used in attacks.

Musk Threat argues that Musk's actions pose a risk to national security. Musk's wealth and influence undermine democracy. Musk's political donations and contracts should be canceled. Putin Connection argues that Musk and Trump have personal interests in crypto and branding with Putin. Musk and Trump take orders from Putin for personal gain. Musk and Trump's connection to Putin is a national security threat. Musk and Trump should be held accountable for their actions supporting Putin. Musk Condemned argues that Musk is criticized for his actions.

@markjacob.bsky.social: “Axis of Evil: Putin, Musk and Trump.”

Musk Threat (40.9%) says Musk is a threat to democracy. Putin Connection (31.1%) says Musk and Trump help Putin. Musk Condemned (28%) says Musk is criticized for his actions.

Russian Aggression argues that Russia funds right-wing politicians to undermine Ukraine. Russia is committing war crimes in Ukraine. Russia is terrorizing Ukrainian civilians. Russia's actions in Ukraine are driven by corporate and individual greed. Trump Russian Asset argues that Trump is controlled by Putin. Trump prioritizes Russia's benefit. Trump acts against US interests for Russia.

@kaybell27.bsky.social: “They are complicit because they are funded by Putin's Russia that bought Trump, Farage, BoJo and many others on the right. These individuals sold out Ukraine for both corporate and individual greed.”

Russian Aggression (68.2%) says Russia is aggressing against Ukraine. Trump Russian Asset (31.8%) says Trump serves Russia's interests.

World.detail:
Iran War argues that US is being manipulated into war with Iran. Iran is fighting back against US allies. US military actions in Iran are harming civilians. War in Iran is a distraction from other issues. Attack on Iran is an elaborate plan to weaken Europe and America. US War Mistake argues that Most posts argue that the US war with Iran is a mistake and has caused harm to the Iranian people and the region.

@theglobaleye.bsky.social: “#BREAKING | 🇺🇸 🇮🇷 — EXCLUSIVE: U.S. source tells The Global Eye, U.S. may strike Iran's Pickaxe Mountain in the next 24 hours.”

Iran War (72%) says US is at war with Iran. US War Mistake (28%) says Most posts argue that the US war with Iran is a mistake and has caused harm to the Iranian people and the region.

Saudi Vulnerability argues that Saudi Arabia has limited options to defeat the Houthis. The Houthis' actions threaten Saudi Arabia's regional leadership. Saudi Arabia's vulnerability undermines its economic power. The conflict with the Houthis affects Saudi Arabia's standing. Yemen Conflict argues that Yemen is one of the worst and most deadly countries. Airstrike kills children in Yemen. Saudi Conflict argues that Saudi military strategy is flawed. Tankers near Saudi Arabia were attacked.

@samfr.bsky.social: “The Saudis really have no way to defeat the Houthis, and there other options aren't great. Many are underestimating the importance of this conflict for the region and the world, given how much Saudi wealth funds...”

Saudi Vulnerability (63.6%) says Saudi Arabia is vulnerable to Houthi attacks. Yemen Conflict (30.3%) says Yemen is experiencing violence and humanitarian crisis. Saudi Conflict (6.1%) says Saudi Arabia faces conflict.

NATO Expansion argues that Putin warned NATO to stop expanding. NATO pushed weapons near Russia. NATO expansion led to invasion. NATO membership would have deterred invasion. NATO expansion was not promised to stop. Starshield Insufficient argues that Starshield is fragile and vulnerable to EMP. Starshield's low orbit makes it easily disrupted by AI-driven EMP weaponry.

@oldsklmarine.bsky.social: “🤔. Oh I don't know. I suppose it when NATO begin pushing missile launchers, and weapon systems against the Russian border in Poland against Belarus and then in the Baltic states.. Putin said back off. NATO rolled their eyes 🙄. They want war”

NATO Expansion (85.7%) says NATO expansion provoked Russia. Starshield Insufficient (14.3%) says Starshield is too weak for NATO use.

Politics.detail:
Katie Zacharia Fired argues that Katie Zacharia's short tenure is a sign of Trump's struggling administration. Zacharia's firing is due to her weakness in representing Trump. Zacharia's lack of qualifications led to her downfall as press secretary. Press Secretary Fired argues that the press secretary did not last long. The press secretary was not properly vetted. The press secretary made Trump look bad.

@ryanlcooper.com: “I guess part of that is a press secretary can only do so much bad stuff, but still”

Katie Zacharia Fired (63.4%) says Katie Zacharia was fired as White House press secretary after five days. Press Secretary Fired (36.6%) says Trump's press secretary was fired.

Trans Rights argues that Labour defends transphobia. People harm trans people. Mainstreaming transness is a disaster. Trans Wales Amazing argues that MP fails to reduce trans discrimination. MP does not represent trans constituents.

@elizabethtaylor47.bsky.social: “Even if you follow the nonsense logic of ‘we’re implementing the SC judgment to reduce abusive transphobia against trans people’ it’s simply wrong in its own terms. Because according to Labour even the most flagrant and overt transphobia is either ignored or outright defended.”

Trans Rights (92.7%) says Trans people lack representation. Trans Wales Amazing (7.3%) says Labour MP faces criticism.

Trump Fires Women argues that Trump fires women for his own mistakes. Incompetent men keep their jobs while women are fired. Trump only fires incompetent women not men. Misogyny Claimed argues that Women are attacked directly and indirectly. Mediocre men cry foul when faced with competent women and minorities. Female grifters don't last as long as male grifters due to prejudice. Women of colour are held to a higher standard than inadequate white men. Trump and Republicans are misogynistic. The administration enables abuse of women. Women Under Attack argues that Men are openly assaulting women at events. Trump only throws women under the bus. Republican women are treated like second class citizens. Men are more likely to commit violent acts against women. The US is a dangerous place for women and non-men.

@badhistorytakes.bsky.social: “If the White House is looking a blonde woman who can lie convincingly, the answer has been right in front of us:”

Trump Fires Women (35.9%) says Trump fires women more than men. Misogyny Claimed (34.6%) says Women are attacked and held to higher standards. Women Under Attack (29.5%) says Women are being assaulted or threatened.

Business.detail:
High Fuel Prices argues that Diesel prices won't decrease. Gas prices are likely to rise again. Russian diesel hasn't lowered pump prices. Fuel prices are too high. Oil Price Surge argues that Iran's attacks on ships are increasing shipping costs. The war in Iran is limiting oil supplies. Conflict in the Strait of Hormuz is reducing crude availability. US crude stockpiles have dropped significantly. The Strait of Hormuz remains a treacherous route for oil tankers.

@english.nv.ua: “🇺🇸 Former Ukrenergo CEO Volodymyr Kudrytskyi said Trump’s plans to buy Russian diesel would have virtually no impact on U.S. fuel prices, arguing that the proposed volumes are too small to influence the American or global market 🔗 📸: Volodymyr Kudrytskyi / Facebook”

High Fuel Prices (71.1%) says Fuel prices will stay high. Oil Price Surge (28.9%) says Oil prices are rising due to conflict.

Financial Struggles argues that Most Americans lack sufficient income. Many cannot afford basic necessities. Debt is widespread among younger Americans. Income Comparison argues that comparing absolute income numbers is misleading. Tax rates and other costs affect income comparisons. Relative income position is more relevant for certain goods. Mixing gross income and tax-free scholarships is incorrect. Income inequality exists even in nonprofit organizations.

@newnarrative.bsky.social: “A majority of Americans (60%) say they don’t have enough income for the kind of life they want. And one-in-five or more say they’ve had trouble paying for medical care, daily transportation, rent or mortgage, or food sometime in the past year.”

Financial Struggles (73.7%) says Many Americans struggle financially. Income Comparison (26.3%) says Income comparisons are misleading.

Musk Deceives argues that Musk spreads lies to inflate stock prices. Musk's promises are unfulfilled and documented. Musk relies on gullible investors. Musk manipulates stocks with false promises. Musk Involved argues that Musk was angered by data center strikes. Musk hired teen hackers to do his bidding.

@lanceparkin.bsky.social: “I mean ... the other problem for Musk is there is an invention called writing, and a lot of the things he's promised were written down complete with prices and delivery dates.”

Musk Deceives (87.5%) says Musk deceives people for financial gain. Musk Involved (12.5%) says Musk was involved in hacking.

Tariff Refunds argues that Big corporations keep tariff refunds. Corporations pocket tariff refunds. US Ties argues that Canada intends to deepen US ties despite tariff talk. A tariff would make US ties acceptable.

@mks231951.bsky.social: “#HeyIowa - ya know those tariff refunds that Trump authorized? They aren’t coming to you and me. Big corporations raised prices that we paid and now big corporations are keeping the refunds. As usual, they profit while we foot the bill.”

Tariff Refunds (69.2%) says Corporations keep tariff refunds. US Ties (30.8%) says Canada pursues deeper ties with US.

Sports.detail:
Inauthentic Support argues that Some fans support teams for selfish reasons. Unfit Owners argues that Vrancken is not a fraud and can help Hearts. Usmanov and Moshiri are unsuitable to own a club.

@dav1dman.bsky.social: “Yep. Could’ve been doing this shit in Fulham or Brentford. All about raising his influencer profile off the back of a random premier league club. The club is irrelevant.”

Inauthentic Support (60%) says Some fans support teams for selfish reasons. Unfit Owners (40%) says Some owners are unfit to own a club.

Dodgers Nlcs Series argues that the Dodgers' high spending creates unfair competition. The claim centers on mercenaries and competition. Postseason Success argues that Postseason pitching is key to success. Regular season performance does not guarantee postseason wins.

@matttomic.bsky.social: “I can't believe the Dodgers. Using their deep-pocket owners to have a salary that overwhelms the competition. Bringing in all sorts of All-Star mercenaries they barely needed. Winning back-to-back World Series. The resulting labor strife leading to a lockout.”

Dodgers Nlcs Series (58.8%) says Dodgers face criticism for their spending. Postseason Success (41.2%) says Postseason success is not solely dependent on regular season performance.

Owner Priorities argues that owners seek passive income. owners may lock out fans. owners are advised by directors. owners want authentic supporter energy. Sports Teams Sold argues that Sports teams are owned by bad people.

@thancredulous.bsky.social: “I've lived in the east bay my whole life and it's fucking criminal that all of our sports teams were sold out, including the warriors, bc people just hate Oakland (Oakland is good. Oakland is fine. I was born there 🥰)”

Owner Priorities (66.7%) says Owners prioritize profits over fans. Sports Teams Sold (33.3%) says Sports teams are owned by bad people.

Game Predictions argues that Ohio State will win against Indiana. Indianapolis Colts will beat Tennessee Titans. Nebraska Oregon needs to be ranked higher. Oklahoma will have an easier road ahead. Game Outcome argues that the game will not go ahead or end in a certain way.

@some-news.bsky.social: “Expert picks, predictions for the marquee top 25 college football games in Week 5”

Game Predictions (66.7%) says Experts predict college football game outcomes. Game Outcome (33.3%) says the game will not go ahead or end in a certain way.

Club Management argues that Club needs better management. Fire Vanni argues that Some fans think Vanni should not be the GM due to poor recruitment and performance.

@perrycaldwell.bsky.social: “I love this. Martin has led from the front for years and a new long-term contract with top wages is fully deserved. Keeping him in North London through his peak is exactly the statement the club needed to make. Let’s get it done.”

Club Management (75%) says Club needs better management. Fire Vanni (25%) says Some fans think Vanni should not be the GM due to poor recruitment and performance.

Culture.detail:
Art Undervalued argues that Support for artists' civic role is mocked. Artists' contributions to society are overlooked. The elite want to control art, not appreciate it. Art World Crisis argues that Artists struggle with AI.

@alecfinlay.bsky.social: “5. Those kinds of projects, with Mar lodge, Trees for Life, and other places, were amongst the most inspiring and socially beneficial work I was involved with.”

Art Undervalued (50%) says Art is undervalued in society. Art World Crisis (50%) says Artists struggle with AI.

Self Publishing argues that Self-published books are not inferior. Self-publishing is not a mistake. Curation biases against self-published authors. Self Publishing Stigma argues that Many authors disagree with the notion that self-published authors are inferior to traditionally published authors.

@owlor.meow.social.ap.brid.gy: “It's also extra funny when people make a distinction between Fanfiction and Real Books when a not insignificant amount of activity among Real Book publishers for the last decade or so has involved taking whatever fanfic is popular, filing off the serial numbers and then…”

Self Publishing (63.6%) says Self-published authors are undervalued. Self Publishing Stigma (36.4%) says Many authors disagree with the notion that self-published authors are inferior to traditionally published authors.

Health.detail:
Care Medical argues that HMOs provide convenient care. Payments may increase aggressive end-of-life care. Medical Neglect argues that Doctors are responsible for harm caused to patients.

@tcoop6231.bsky.social: “Everyone likes to hate on HMOs but they’re literally the best option in the private marketplace. All my medical care comes from one facility within walking distance of my house.”

Care Medical (66.7%) says HMOs are the best option. Medical Neglect (33.3%) says Doctors are responsible for harm caused to patients.

Hospital Billing argues that Hospital master charge lists are entirely made up. Hospital charges are not based in reality. Hospitals charge for fake costs like skin to skin contact. Hospitals hold patients to inflated debt for years. Charges Are Fake argues that Some posts argue that hospital charges are not based on real costs, but rather made-up or inflated numbers.

@yourpaljohn.bsky.social: “Medical charges, the numbers every expert knows are real”

Hospital Billing (60%) says Hospital charges are often fake or made up. Charges Are Fake (40%) says Some posts argue that hospital charges are not based on real costs, but rather made-up or inflated numbers.

Distrust Patients argues that Patients are often not believed. NICU Costs argues that 45 minute surgical room stay costs over $35000. insurance covered the expensive room cost. long NICU stay could be extremely costly.

@laceslibgremlin.bsky.social: “I don’t like how comfortable people online are with accusing people of faking illnesses now I keep most of my medical history offline because at this point no armchair self-appointed doctor would believe it but that’s not going to change how my blood tests come back, now is it?”

Distrust Patients (60%) says Patients are often not believed. NICU Costs (40%) says Hospital stays are very expensive.

Environment.detail:
Climate Change argues that Business interests suppress climate concerns. Climate change is not a hoax. Climate action is needed now. Carbon Sequestration argues that Nuclear power is not a solution to the climate crisis.

@alisheridan.bsky.social: “"We are witnessing the rapid destabilization of the Earth's climate system. This is no longer a warning for the future; it is a diagnosis of the present.”

Climate Change (93.5%) says Climate change is happening now. Carbon Sequestration (6.5%) says Nuclear power is not a solution to the climate crisis.

Data Center Power argues that Data centers should be powered by renewable energy plants. Wind power should prioritize public infrastructure over data centers. Nuclear plants can be revived to power data centers. No Data Centres argues that UK does not need data centres. Data centres are unnecessary.

@oliver48.bsky.social: “Let alone worldwide climate change + El Nino food growing devastation, and hundreds of water guzzling data centres ... "Growing food price fears as water firms blamed for drought and sewage failures" morningstaronline.co.uk/article/grow...”

Data Center Power (88.9%) says Data centers should use renewable energy. No Data Centres (11.1%) says Data centres are not needed.

Climate Debate argues that UK Parliament to debate climate and nature risks. Government to discuss climate emergency and risks. Climate emergency debate scheduled for November 16th. El Nino Effects argues that El Nino brings drought and flood. El Nino will bring heavy rain and mudslides. Indonesia Burning argues that Politicians are not addressing Indonesia's heat and wildfires. Forest fires in Indonesia are causing human suffering.

@rumlockerart.bsky.social: “We're currently having intense drought & flood+landslide at the same time in the same country thanks to this el nino. Many Volcanoes erupted and still in alert status. Borneo currently burning and the haze is causing big trouble (you can google this yourself).”

Climate Debate (40%) says UK Parliament will debate climate risks. El Nino Effects (40%) says El Nino causes extreme weather. Indonesia Burning (20%) says Indonesia is getting hotter due to wildfires.

Solar Limitations argues that relying solely on solar is an engineering gamble. solar panels can hinder crop growth. batteries cannot solve seasonal solar output drops. Clean Energy argues that Clean energy creates good-paying jobs. Carbon-free energy is a significant portion of the grid.

@lovenuclear.com: “2/14 In a world where the climate is actively changing, betting the entire economy on wind, solar and batteries without a credible plan for prolonged low-output periods is an absurd engineering gamble.”

Solar Limitations (71.4%) says Solar power has limitations. Clean Energy (28.6%) says Clean energy is important for the future.

Human Wildlife Conflict argues that Elephant food banks can curb human-wildlife conflict. Reducing food waste can improve human well-being. Hunting Ban argues that puffin hunt is cruel. hunting at close range is cruel.

@corq.bsky.social: “Russia fears 'invasion' as hungry wolves reach Moscow and deemed 'threat to people' - Daily Star Well, wouldn't that be a shame? For the wolves digestion tracts, I mean...”

Human Wildlife Conflict (62.5%) says Humans and wildlife are in conflict. Hunting Ban (37.5%) says Hunting practices are cruel.

Education.detail:
Private Schools argues that private education is unfamiliar to many. interpreting national trends is challenging due to private schools. Education Bias argues that Students in non-mainstream settings face stigma. Some colleges are unprepared for students with non-traditional backgrounds. Additional support is crucial for students' success. Prestigious schools may be graduating unqualified students.

@isabellefk.bsky.social: “Yes, it must be a really tricky & diverse group. It also doesn’t get picked up eg in those PISA data, Ofsted reports etc because they all rely on people being in settings. So there’s already a bias or gap in what we think we know about edu for YP.”

Private Schools (50%) says Private schools are different. Education Bias (50%) says Education system has biases.

Math Education argues that teaching problem solving is important. Students must think to achieve stronger outcomes. Direct instruction hinders mathematical thinking. Schools Faulted argues that Schools cause bodily harm beyond brain damage. Schools fail to provide qualified teachers in key subjects.

@rosser-gooner.bsky.social: “It's so stupid. Teaching people to problem solve is as important, whether they use that specific maths in the future or not.”

Math Education (69.2%) says Math education should focus on problem solving. Schools Faulted (30.8%) says Schools harm students physically.

Parenting Fails argues that Parents offload basics on schools. Not all parents have equal social capital. School Funding argues that School funding favors wealthy families.

@nuitsdeyoung.bsky.social: “No. I'm saying that a lot of parents appear to be offloading basics of parenting on to schools.”

Parenting Fails (50%) says Parents offload responsibilities on schools. School Funding (50%) says School funding favors wealthy families.
